cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, code or paper, please cite it as below."
title: "AI Governance Atlas: From AI Principles to Regulatory Practice"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Suzzanpatel"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Suzzanpatel/ai-governance-atlas"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, provision-level comparison of how the European Union, India and
  the United Kingdom translate AI governance principles into enforceable
  obligations, using the OECD AI Principles as an international benchmark.
  Includes the coded evidence dataset, the analysis pipeline, a generated
  academic paper and an interactive dashboard.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI regulation
  - EU AI Act
  - India
  - United Kingdom
  - OECD AI Principles
  - comparative law
  - computational legal studies
